  "description": "PIZSEY crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C62 H72 Ho6 N12 O28 4+,4(Cl1 1-),2(C1 H4 O1),10(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Ho2 (Ho) has 7 O neighbors; Ho1 (Ho) has 7 O neighbors; Ho3 (Ho) has 7 O neighbors; Ho4 (Ho) has 7 O neighbors; Ho5 (Ho) has 7 O neighbors; Ho6 (Ho) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.610-3.975 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.88-114.41°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C64H100Cl4Ho6N12O40. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
